Hi Chris,

That is the default behavior.  I will have to let Wei-Chen speak to the particulars, but I think the idea is to make it very easy to install for the end user, particularly on Windows.

You can use the (basically undocumented) configure option --enable-ld-library-path, the effect of which can be seen in R/zzz.r.in <http://zzz.r.in>.  I've been meaning to expand on how this works and why someone might want it in the vignette, but haven't gotten around to it.

Thanks
-Drew

